OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F306A1786114088
OL,3,CDowning Street vows to help pubs
OL,4,Cthrive amid 'vertical-drinking' row
OL,6,FDowning Street has weighed in on a row
OL,7,Fover limiting standing-up drinking
OL,8,Foutside London pubs, calling on local
OL,9,Fcouncils to help the industry
OL,10,F"continue to thrive".
OL,12,FIt comes after Westminster City
OL,13,FCouncil published a draft set of
OL,14,Falcohol policies, encouraging bar
OL,15,Fstaff to put out tables and chairs in
OL,16,Fplace of space to drink standing up.
OL,18,FWestminster City Council's draft
OL,19,Fstatement of licensing policy includes
OL,20,Fan intention to "discourage excessive
OL,21,Fdrunkenness".
OL,26,@|D@QOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G1/15
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,307,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30602
SC,0002
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F306A1786114088
OL,3,CDowning Street vows to help pubs
OL,4,Cthrive amid 'vertical-drinking' row
OL,6,FThe draft policy is also designed to
OL,7,F"encourage provision of more seating
OL,8,Fin premises that serve alcohol for
OL,9,Fpeople to sit and enjoy a drink and
OL,10,Forder food by table service in place
OL,11,Fof open bar space that caters for high
OL,12,Fvolume vertical drinking".
OL,14,FOne policy, numbered CIP1, is to
OL,15,F"normally refuse" pub, bar, fast food
OL,16,For music venue licences in an area
OL,17,Fknown as the West End cumulative
OL,18,Fimpact zone ` the area roughly between
OL,19,FOxford Street and Trafalgar Square,
OL,20,Ftaking in Leicester Square and Soho.
OL,26,@tD@YO]wD@AOUwD@QO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G2/15
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,307,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30603
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F306A1786114088
OL,3,CDowning Street vows to help pubs
OL,4,Cthrive amid 'vertical-drinking' row
OL,6,F"The introduction of measures to
OL,7,Freduce the extent of, or to remove
OL,8,Fopportunities for, vertical drinking
OL,9,Fcould address the underlying reasons
OL,10,Ffor the policy," the document reads.
OL,12,FPaul Swaddle, the council's
OL,13,FConservative leader, has insisted
OL,14,F"there is no plan" to stop "vertical
OL,15,Fdrinking" in his borough, however,
OL,16,Finsisting the policies are out for
OL,17,Fconsultation, with the council's
OL,18,Fsurvey due to close on Sunday August 9.
OL,26,@nD@AOUrD@PO]vD@AOUvD@RO]vD@\OUwD@IO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/15
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,307,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30604
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F306A1786114088
OL,3,CDowning Street vows to help pubs
OL,4,Cthrive amid 'vertical-drinking' row
OL,6,FCouncillor Swaddle accused the press
OL,7,Fof writing "confusing stories" about
OL,8,Fwhat the document meant and added: "I
OL,9,Fwant to be straight with people.
OL,11,F"There is no plan, and never has been,
OL,12,Fto ban drinking while standing up in a
OL,13,FWestminster pub."
OL,15,FNo 10 appeared to side with pub
OL,16,Flandlords when asked about the row,
OL,17,Fwith a Downing Street spokesperson
OL,18,Fsaying: "Busy pubs full of people
OL,19,Ftalking to each other is not a public
OL,20,Fnuisance, it is British life and it is
OL,21,Fthousands of jobs.
OL,26,@oD@LOUoD@^O]pD@dOUsD@AOUuD@QO]zD@IOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G4/15
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,307,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30605
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F306A1786114088
OL,3,CDowning Street vows to help pubs
OL,4,Cthrive amid 'vertical-drinking' row
OL,6,F"The government is devolving new
OL,7,Flicensing powers to the Mayor to help
OL,8,Fsupport pubs and nightlife. Soho did
OL,9,Fnot become world famous by taking last
OL,10,Forders early, switching the lights off
OL,11,Fat 10 o'clock.
OL,13,F"The prime minister encourages local
OL,14,Fleaders to work with the industry so
OL,15,Fthat pubs can continue to thrive."
OL,17,FPrime Minister Andy Burnham has
OL,18,Fpreviously vowed to be "a defender"
OL,19,Ffor British pubs when he visited a pub
OL,20,Fin Essex last month.
OL,26,@nD@AOUuD@AOUwD@bO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G5/15
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
